  "description": "The Durmitor is shaped by the practical demands of fast road riding. Its geometry favours decisive handling and immediate response, creating a bike that feels closely connected to the rider. Nothing is added for effect; each element serves a clear purpose.\n\nOur take on the modern road bike: fast, precise and focused. Built for hard road rides, fast solo efforts, group rides and chasing the feeling of a bike that wants to move.\n\nDurmitor keeps the frame clean and purposeful. No unnecessary mounts, no added clutter, no attempt to be everything at once. The result is a road bike with a clear brief: low, fast, precise and refined.\n\nPaired with the ENVE Road In-Route fork, keeping the front end clean, aerodynamic and focused. It supports the bike’s road-race intent while giving a complete integrated cockpit system. The fork, frame and painted-to-match stem are designed to read as one system.\n\nConstructed with real world riding in mind. With clearance for 35c tyres but geometry to support a longer, lower position; the Durmitor is composed to reward committed riding without becoming twitchy or nervous.\n\nThe most stripped-back bike in the range. It does not need fussy accessory mounts or extra features to justify itself. Its purpose is simple: a fast, modern road bike, made in London, with every detail serving that brief.\n\nWhat defines the Durmitor is its focus. The design is refined until only what matters remains, resulting in a bike that feels precise and settled from the first ride. It is built as a cohesive whole, engineered in depth but experienced simply.",
